## Props

An `<article>` whose heading is a real link stretched over the card. Figure, summary and status read in order.

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `title` (required) | `string` |  | What this card is about, such as "Decisions". It is the link text and the card's heading. |
| `summary` (required) | `React.ReactNode` |  | The takeaway sentence, such as "2 need you by Thursday". |
| `figure` | `React.ReactNode` |  | One glanceable figure, such as "2" or "$420". |
| `status` | `{ tone: StatusTone; label: string }` |  | A status word, always spelled out. The tone adds color to it. |
| `href` | `string` |  | Where the next level lives. The whole card is the link's target. |
| `headingLevel` | `2 \| 3 \| 4` | `3` | Heading level. Default 3. |
| `className` | `string` |  |  |

These props use types from other items:

- `StatusTone` is `ToneSubset<'neutral' | 'positive' | 'caution' | 'critical'>`, declared in [`lede-utils`](lede-utils.md#types).

## Example

The smallest working use, from the docs site:

```tsx
import { SummaryCard } from '@/components/lede/blocks/summary-card';

export function DecisionsCard({ due }: { due: number }) {
  return (
    <SummaryCard
      title="Decisions"
      figure={due}
      summary="Both due by Thursday."
      status={{ tone: 'caution', label: 'Needs you' }}
      href="/decisions"
    />
  );
}
```

Docs: [Blocks](https://lede.cloudcompute.com/blocks.md).

